  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p><strong>AURA</strong> faint evocation; <strong>CL</strong> 5th <strong>SLOT</strong> neck; <strong>PRICE</strong> 4,000 gp (+1), 16,000 gp (+2), 36,000 gp (+3), 64,000 gp (+4), 100,000 (+5) gp; <strong>WEIGHT</strong> -</p>\n<p><strong>DESCRIPTION</strong><br>\nThis copper pot, worn on the head, grants an enhancement bonus of +1 to +5 on attack and damage rolls with improvised melee weapons.</p>\n<p>Alternatively, this copper head pot can grant improvised melee weapon special abilities. See Table: Melee Weapon Special Abilities in the Pathfinder Core Rulebook for a list of abilities. Special abilities count as additional bonuses for determining the market value of the item, but do not modify attack or damage bonuses. A head pot of adequate trash cannot have a modified bonus (enhancement bonus plus special ability bonus equivalents) higher than +5. A head pot of adequate trash does not need to have a +1 enhancement bonus to grant an improvised melee weapon special ability.</p>\n<p><strong>CONSTRUCTION REQUIREMENTS</strong><br>\nCraft Wondrous Item, greater magic weapon, creator’s caster level must be at least three times the amulet’s bonus, plus any requirements of the melee weapon special abilities; <strong>COST</strong> 2,000 gp (+1), 8,000 gp (+2), 18,000 gp (+3), 32,000 gp (+4), 50,000 gp (+5)</p>\n<p><a href=\"http://spheresofpower.wikidot.com/gonzo-wondrous-items#toc5\">Source: Spheres of Power Wiki</a></p>",
